<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">

  <!--
    Nop.Plugin.Pickup.PickupInStore - task 13.1
    (Requirements 5.5, 1.1-1.5, 2.4, 4.2, 4.3, 4.4, 5.1, 5.3, 3.1).

    THE RECIPE THIS FOLLOWS is the annotated
    src/Plugins/Nop.Plugin.DiscountRules.CustomerRoles/Nop.Plugin.DiscountRules.CustomerRoles.csproj
    (task 10.1). Read that file for the reasoning behind the five silently-failing decisions
    (SDK.Razor + AddRazorSupportForMvc; the Content/Link view-resolution block; Private="false"
    plus the NopPluginDoNotDeployHostAssemblies target; AppendTargetFrameworkToOutputPath=false;
    and Content Include vs Update for non-.cshtml content). Only what is DIFFERENT about this
    plugin is documented here.

    ===================================================================================
    WHAT IS DIFFERENT - THIS PLUGIN HAS ITS OWN DbContext (runtime deferral 4.10)
    ===================================================================================
    Data\StorePickupPointObjectContext.cs is an EF context of its own, registered by
    DependencyRegistrar through Nop.Web.Framework's RegisterPluginDataContext. It is one of the
    four plugin contexts deferral 4.10 names (the third to be ported, after Feed.GoogleShopping
    at 11.2), and it is why this project references Nop.Data DIRECTLY - the legacy project did
    too, alongside EF6 <Reference>s (EntityFramework 6.1.3 + EntityFramework.SqlServer) that are
    NOT restated here: EF6 has no place in this solution any more and EF Core arrives
    transitively through Nop.Data (task 3.1). Its Install() calls
    Nop.Data.DbContextExtensions.ExecuteSqlScript, which splits the GO-batched EF Core create
    script (see the context file). Worked example: Nop.Plugin.Feed.GoogleShopping (11.2).

    This plugin ships NO static asset tree (no Content/ or Scripts/ folder referenced by
    ~/Plugins/... URL), so it needs no NopStaticFileProvider allow-list entry - unlike
    Feed.GoogleShopping / ExternalAuth.Facebook / Widgets.NivoSlider.

    ===================================================================================
    DROPPED IN THE CLASSIC -> SDK CONVERSION (Requirements 1.4, 1.5)
    ===================================================================================
    As in the 10.1 template: ToolsVersion/DefaultTargets/xmlns, ProjectGuid, ProductVersion,
    SchemaVersion, FileAlignment, AppDesignerFolder, OutputType, TargetFrameworkProfile,
    NuGetPackageImportStamp, TargetFrameworkVersion v4.5.1, Prefer32Bit, ErrorReport,
    WarningLevel, DefineConstants and the Debug/Release DebugType/DebugSymbols/Optimize blocks;
    the explicit <Compile Include> list of 12 files; the Microsoft.CSharp.targets import, the
    Microsoft.Bcl.Build.targets import and its EnsureNuGetPackageBuildImports guard, and the
    commented BeforeBuild/AfterBuild stubs.

    Every <Reference> with a HintPath into ..\..\packages\ is gone: the Microsoft.AspNet.Mvc
    5.2.3 / WebPages 3.2.3 System.Web MVC stack (System.Web.Mvc / System.Web.WebPages), Autofac
    4.4.0 (transitive now), EntityFramework + EntityFramework.SqlServer (EF6, see above). The BCL
    <Reference>s (Microsoft.CSharp, System, System.Core) are subsumed by the net10.0 shared
    framework, and <Reference Include="System.Web" /> has no net10.0 counterpart at all.

    app.config, packages.config and web.config are DELETED; web.config's load-bearing content
    (pageBaseType + the four System.Web namespaces) is transcribed to Views/_ViewImports.cshtml.
    Properties/AssemblyInfo.cs is KEPT (GenerateAssemblyInfo=false is solution-wide, task 2.3, so
    deleting it would drop AssemblyVersion to 0.0.0.0). Notes.txt stays non-deployed Content, as
    in 3.90.

    NOTE the legacy logo file is logo.png here (most plugins ship logo.jpg); it is deployed
    verbatim under its own name.

    No <PackageReference>: this plugin has no third-party dependency of its own once EF6 is gone.
    TargetFramework/Nullable/ImplicitUsings/GenerateAssemblyInfo come from
    src/Directory.Build.props; net10.0 is restated so it is verifiable from this file (Req 1.2).
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <AddRazorSupportForMvc>true</AddRazorSupportForMvc>
    <StaticWebAssetsEnabled>false</StaticWebAssetsEnabled>
    <OutputPath>..\..\Presentation\Nop.Web\Plugins\Pickup.PickupInStore\</OutputPath>
    <AppendTargetFrameworkToOutputPath>false</AppendTargetFrameworkToOutputPath>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    Required explicitly - Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor does not add it implicitly. The controller
    binds Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc (+ .Rendering for SelectListItem), the route provider binds
    Microsoft.AspNetCore.Routing / .Builder (IEndpointRouteBuilder, MapControllerRoute) and the
    plugin class binds Microsoft.AspNetCore.Routing (RouteValueDictionary, on
    IPickupPointProvider.GetConfigurationRoute).
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <FrameworkReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.App" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Libraries\Nop.Core\Nop.Core.csproj" Private="false" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Libraries\Nop.Data\Nop.Data.csproj" Private="false" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Libraries\Nop.Services\Nop.Services.csproj" Private="false" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Presentation\Nop.Web.Framework\Nop.Web.Framework.csproj" Private="false" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Private="false" alone is NOT sufficient - see runtime-deferrals.md section 83.3. Like
    Feed.GoogleShopping this plugin references Nop.Data DIRECTLY, so Nop.Data.dll would be copied
    here by name rather than by transitive accident, and PluginManager would shadow-copy and load
    it as the process's Nop.Data. Verbatim from the template; the "Nop." prefix filter keeps
    Payments.PayPalDirect's private PayPal SDK working (task 12.3).
  -->
  <Target Name="NopPluginDoNotDeployHostAssemblies" AfterTargets="ResolveReferences">
    <ItemGroup>
      <ReferenceCopyLocalPaths
          Remove="@(ReferenceCopyLocalPaths)"
          Condition="$([System.String]::Copy('%(Filename)').StartsWith('Nop.'))" />
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>

  <!--
    View resolution. %(Link) becomes the compiled Razor identifier, so each view compiles as
    /Plugins/Pickup.PickupInStore/Views/... and the controller's
    View("~/Plugins/Pickup.PickupInStore/Views/Xyz.cshtml", model) call sites stay UNEDITED.
    %(RecursiveDir) already contains "Views/" - do not repeat it. CopyToOutputDirectory="Never":
    the views live inside the dll now, a deployed copy is dead weight AND Link would place it at
    the wrong path. This is also what keeps Views/Configure.cshtml free of any _ViewStart: its
    ancestors under /Plugins/... have none, which is correct for an admin panel (deferral 83.1).
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <Content Update="Views\**\*.cshtml"
             Link="Plugins\Pickup.PickupInStore\%(RecursiveDir)%(Filename)%(Extension)"
             CopyToOutputDirectory="Never" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Runtime-read content, deployed exactly as in 3.90. Include, NOT Update - AND the <None Remove>
    first; under Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor the default Content glob covers only .cshtml/.razor, so a
    bare <Content Update="Description.txt"> would match NOTHING and PluginManager could not see
    the plugin at all.

      Description.txt   parsed by PluginManager.Initialize; SupportedVersions must contain
                        NopVersion.CurrentVersion ("3.90"). Asserted, not assumed, by
                        Nop.Web.SmokeTests.PluginViewRenderTests.
      logo.png          shown by the admin plugin list; CopyToOutputDirectory="Always" as in 3.90.
      Notes.txt         3.90 declared it Content with no CopyToOutputDirectory, i.e. not deployed.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Remove="Description.txt" />
    <None Remove="logo.png" />
    <None Remove="Notes.txt" />
    <Content Include="Description.txt" CopyToOutputDirectory="PreserveNewest" />
    <Content Include="logo.png" CopyToOutputDirectory="Always" />
    <Content Include="Notes.txt" CopyToOutputDirectory="Never" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
